Description: Keep a declared stereo pair out of physical screen segmentation
 A two-view buffer is not a desktop rectangle. The physical screen weave
 crops and repacks it again when it intersects a second output.
 Stereo KWin owns placement and output filtering of the declared pair.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos
Origin: other, Sparky Stereo OS runtime fork
Forwarded: no, to be offered to DisplayXR after their open pull request settles
Last-Update: 2026-11-21

diff --git a/src/xrt/compositor/vk_native/comp_vk_native_compositor.c b/src/xrt/compositor/vk_native/comp_vk_native_compositor.c
index d09ed3e2c..ea3f1a737 100644
--- a/src/xrt/compositor/vk_native/comp_vk_native_compositor.c
+++ b/src/xrt/compositor/vk_native/comp_vk_native_compositor.c
@@ -6594,6 +6594,13 @@ vk_segments_frame_update_split(struct comp_vk_native_compositor *c,
                                bool *out_would_split)
 {
 	*out_would_split = false;
+	// A declared pair is a buffer for the desktop compositor, not a physical
+	// screen weave. Its two-view width is not a desktop rectangle: segmenting
+	// it against screen coordinates crops and packs the eyes a second time.
+	// Stereo KWin owns output placement and filtering for this declaration.
+	if (c->full_sbs.declared) {
+		return false;
+	}
 	if (c->seg_screens == NULL || c->display_processor == NULL || c->cmd_pool == VK_NULL_HANDLE ||
 	    !c->have_seg_window) {
 		return false;
